cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "neuro-fpga: a bit-level verified fixed-point LIF neuron and 256-neuron spiking network on a Tang Nano 20K"
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: ChiaAn
    affiliation: "Master Program for Health and Intelligent Medicine, National Taiwan University"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24013358
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KiraIch/fpga-lif-snn"
keywords:
  - spiking neural network
  - leaky integrate-and-fire
  - fixed-point arithmetic
  - FPGA
  - Tang Nano 20K
  - Gowin GW2AR-18
abstract: >-
  Verilog RTL, Python reference model, and host scripts for a leaky
  integrate-and-fire neuron and a 256-neuron time-multiplexed network on a
  Tang Nano 20K (Gowin GW2AR-18). The hardware is checked against a fixed-point
  Python model, in simulation and on the board.
